  <h3 id="what-it-is">What the Gumroad connector is</h3>
  <p>Gumroad runs a server that speaks MCP (Model Context Protocol), so an AI assistant that supports MCP can work with your store from your chat. You connect your Gumroad account once, sign in through Gumroad, and then you can ask the assistant things like "show my recent sales" or "draft a product called Photo Pack for $12".</p>
  <p>Nothing about your store changes. Products, customers, sales, and payouts all stay in Gumroad, and customers still pay through Gumroad checkout. The connector is a way to read your store's data and make a few changes from chat instead of from your dashboard.</p>

  <h3 id="availability">Which assistants you can connect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Claude:</strong> available now as a custom connector. Your Claude plan or your organization's settings have to allow custom connectors.</li>
    <li><strong>Muse:</strong> submitted for review. The Gumroad connector is not yet available in Muse.</li>
    <li><strong>ChatGPT:</strong> not available yet. We will announce it when it is.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Setup instructions for every assistant we support are also at <a href="https://gumroad.com/mcp">gumroad.com/mcp</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="connect-claude">Connecting Claude</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>In Claude, open <strong>Settings &gt; Connectors</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Add custom connector</strong>, then paste this URL: <code>https://gumroad.com/claude/v1/mcp</code></li>
    <li>If you do not see the option to add a custom connector, your plan or your organization administrator controls it.</li>
    <li>When Claude opens a Gumroad sign-in page, sign in and review the permissions you are asked to grant.</li>
    <li>In a chat, select the Gumroad connector and try asking "Show my Gumroad products."</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Your assistant can only see the Gumroad account you signed in with. If you sell from more than one account, connect the one you want to work with.</p>

  <h3 id="can-do">What your assistant can do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Read your name, username, storefront URL, and currency.</li>
    <li>List your products, newest first, with their prices, including pay-what-you-want minimum and suggested prices.</li>
    <li>Read a single product's description and, with sales access, its sales count and revenue.</li>
    <li>Create a new product as an unpublished draft.</li>
    <li>Publish or unpublish a product you own.</li>
    <li>List your recent sales, including the buyer's email address, the product, the amount, and the time.</li>
    <li>List your recent payouts and their status.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Drafts created from chat have no files attached. Add the files in Gumroad and check the name, price, and description before you publish anything.</p>

  <h3 id="cannot-do">What your assistant cannot do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Take a payment or run checkout. Customers always pay through Gumroad.</li>
    <li>Upload files, covers, or content to a product.</li>
    <li>Refund a sale, or change your payout destination or payout schedule.</li>
    <li>Delete a product.</li>
    <li>Change a product's price or description after it exists. Only a draft's name, price, and description can be set, and that is at the moment it is created.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Anything outside that list, do in your Gumroad dashboard.</p>

  <h3 id="permissions">What you are granting access to</h3>
  <p>The connector asks for permission for the specific things it needs. You can grant some and not others:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Public profile</strong> and <strong>profile</strong>: your name, username, and storefront basics.</li>
    <li><strong>Products</strong>: read your products, create drafts, and publish or unpublish them.</li>
    <li><strong>Sales</strong>: read your recent sales, including buyer email addresses.</li>
    <li><strong>Payouts</strong>: read your payout amounts and status.</li>
    <li><strong>Account</strong>: full access to your account, which is wider than the connector needs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Sales access means the assistant can read your customers' email addresses, so grant it only if you are comfortable with that. If you deny a permission, the assistant simply cannot use the tools that need it and will say which one it is missing.</p>

  <h3 id="revoke">Revoking access</h3>
  <p>Revoke the connection any time under <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings/authorized_applications">Authorized Applications</a> in your Gumroad settings. Disconnecting or deleting the connector inside your AI app does not revoke its access token, so revoke it in Gumroad to actually end the connection.</p>

  <h3 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h3>
  <p><strong>I cannot find "Add custom connector" in Claude.</strong> Custom connectors depend on your Claude plan and your organization's settings. If you are on a team plan, an administrator may need to enable them for you.</p>
  <p><strong>The assistant says it cannot find my products.</strong> Check that you connected the Gumroad account that owns them, and that you granted product access during sign-in. If you connected the wrong account, revoke access and connect again.</p>
  <p><strong>A tool says it needs a permission.</strong> Reconnect the assistant and grant the permission it names. Nothing else changes when you do.</p>
  <p><strong>Publishing from chat fails.</strong> Publishing needs the same things it needs in your dashboard: a confirmed email address, payouts set up for your account, and shipping destinations if you sell physical products. A product that Gumroad has taken down also cannot be published. Fix that in Gumroad, then ask the assistant to publish again.</p>
  <p><strong>The assistant created a draft I cannot sell.</strong> Drafts start with no files. Add your files to the product in Gumroad, then publish it there or ask the assistant to publish it.</p>
  <p>If something else is not working, email <a href="mailto:support@gumroad.com">support@gumroad.com</a> and tell us which assistant you connected.</p>
